{
  "original_id": "lit-260905848-p01",
  "archive_id": "BW2-L260905848-P01",
  "title": "An Exact Computer-Assisted Resolution of the Binary (n,k,r)=(5,3,3) Frankl–Tokushige Instance",
  "batch_label": "本地文献跟进",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Let V = F_2^5. For i = 1,2,3 let F_i be a family of 3-dimensional linear subspaces of V, and suppose dim(U_1 intersection U_2 intersection U_3) >= 1 for every choice U_i in F_i. Then |F_1||F_2||F_3| <= 35^3 = 42875. Equality holds if and only if there is a 1-dimensional subspace L <= V such that, for every i, F_i is the full star of all 3-subspaces containing L.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
